Netflix Data Analysis using Python, SQL & Power BI

Author: Merline Princy

Tools Used: Python, Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, Seaborn, SQL (MySQL), Power BI

Abstract

The entertainment industry generates vast amounts of data that can be analyzed to understand audience preferences and content strategies. This project analyzes the Netflix Movies and TV Shows dataset using Python, SQL, and Power BI. The objective is to explore Netflix's content library, identify trends across genres, ratings, countries, directors, and release years, and build an interactive dashboard to support business decision-making.

1. Introduction

Netflix is one of the world's largest streaming platforms, offering thousands of movies and TV shows across multiple countries and languages.

Analyzing Netflix's content library helps answer important business questions such as:

What type of content dominates the platform?
Which countries contribute the most content?
Which genres are most popular?
How has Netflix's content library evolved over time?
What are the dominant audience ratings?

The project combines data cleaning, exploratory data analysis (EDA), SQL querying, and dashboard development to generate meaningful business insights.

2. Objectives

The objectives of this project are:

Clean and preprocess the Netflix dataset.
Perform exploratory data analysis (EDA).
Analyze trends across countries, ratings, genres, and release years.
Develop SQL queries for business analysis.
Create an interactive Power BI dashboard.
Generate actionable business insights and recommendations.
3. Dataset Description

Dataset Name: Netflix Movies and TV Shows

Source: Kaggle

File Used: netflix1.csv

Number of Records: Approximately 8,790

Number of Columns: 10

The dataset contains information about:

Content Type
Title
Director
Country
Date Added
Release Year
Rating
Duration
Genres
